    3233:   // NOTE: I claim that this chunk of the algorithm (the looping part) needs to
    3234:   // run the loop at MOST NumItems() times.  This claim should hold up
    3235:   // because we'll freeze at least one item on each loop iteration, and once
    3236:   // we've run out of items to freeze, there's nothing left to do.  However,
    3237:   // in most cases, we'll break out of this loop long before we hit that many
    3238:   // iterations.
    3239:   for (uint32_t iterationCounter = 0; iterationCounter < NumItems();
    3240:        iterationCounter++) {
    3241:     // Set every not-yet-frozen item's used main size to its
    3242:     // flex base size, and subtract all the used main sizes from our
    3243:     // total amount of space to determine the 'available free space'
    3244:     // (positive or negative) to be distributed among our flexible items.
    3245:     AuCoord64 availableFreeSpace = spaceAvailableForFlexItemsContentBoxes;
